batch_outputs:   20%|#9        | 99/500 [17:07<2:20:22, 21.00s/it][["\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 926 and 124?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of 926 and 124 step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 926 by 4 (the ones place of 124):**\n   \\[\n   926 \\times 4 = 3,\\!704\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 926 by 20 (the tens place of 124):**\n   \\[\n   926 \\times 20 = 18,\\!520\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 926 by 100 (the hundreds place of 124):**\n   \\[\n   926 \\times 100 = 92,\\!600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   3,\\!704 + 18,\\!520 + 92,\\!600 = 114,\\!824\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 926 and 124 is \\(\\boxed{114,\\!824}\\).", "114,824.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me check my calculations again.\n\nStarting over, multiplying 926 by 4 gives 3,704.\n\nMultiplying 926 by 20 gives 18,520.\n\nMultiplying 926 by 100 gives 92,600.\n\nNow, adding these together: 3,704 plus 18,520 is 22,224. Adding 92,600 to that gives a total of 114,824.\n\nHmm, that still doesn't feel correct. Let me try a different approach.\n\nAlternatively, I can break down 124 into 100 + 20 + 4.\n\nMultiplying 926 by 100 gives 92,600.\n\nMultiplying 926 by 20 gives 18,520.\n\nMultiplying 926 by 4 gives 3,704.\n\nAdding these together: 92,600 plus 18,520 is 111,120. Adding 3,704 to that results in 114,824.\n\nWait, I'm getting the same answer again. Maybe I was correct the first time. Let me verify using another method.\n\nIf I multiply 926 by 124 directly:\n\n926 × 124\n\n= 926 × (100 + 20 + 4)\n\n= 926 × 100 + 926 × 20 + 926 × 4\n\n= 92,600 + 18,520 + 3,704\n\n= 92,600 + 18,520 = 111,120\n\n111,120 + 3,704 = 114,824\n\nYes, that confirms it. The correct product of 926 and 124 is 114,824.\n"]]
