batch_outputs:  [["\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 255 and 573?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of 255 and 573 step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 255 by the ones place digit (3) of 573:**\n   \\[\n   255 \\times 3 = 765\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 255 by the tens place digit (70) of 573:**\n   \\[\n   255 \\times 70 = 17,850\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 255 by the hundreds place digit (500) of 573:**\n   \\[\n   255 \\times 500 = 127,500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   765 + 17,850 + 127,500 = 145,755\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{145,\\!755}\\).", "145,755.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 765 plus 17,850 plus 127,500 equals 145,755.\n"]]
