batch_outputs:  [["\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 203 and 373?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of 203 and 373 step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 203 by 3 (ones place of 373):**\n   \\[\n   203 \\times 3 = 609\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 203 by 70 (tens place of 373):**\n   \\[\n   203 \\times 70 = 14,210\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 203 by 300 (hundreds place of 373):**\n   \\[\n   203 \\times 300 = 60,900\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   609 + 14,210 + 60,900 = 75,719\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 203 and 373 is \\(\\boxed{75,\\!719}\\).", "75,719.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nStarting over, multiplying 203 by 3 gives 609.\n\nMultiplying 203 by 70 gives 14,210.\n\nMultiplying 203 by 300 gives 60,900.\n\nAdding these together: 609 + 14,210 = 14,819, and then 14,819 + 60,900 = 75,719.\n\nHmm, that still doesn't match my initial thought. Maybe I made a mistake in the multiplication steps.\n\nLet me try another approach. I'll break down 373 into 300 + 70 + 3.\n\nMultiplying 203 by 300: 203 × 300 = 60,900.\n\nMultiplying 203 by 70: 203 × 70 = 14,210.\n\nMultiplying 203 by 3: 203 × 3 = 609.\n\nAdding these results: 60,900 + 14,210 = 75,110, and then 75,110 + 609 = 75,719.\n\nIt seems consistent. Therefore, the correct product of 203 and 373 is 75,719.\n"]]
