batch_outputs:  [["\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 764 and 397?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of 764 and 397 step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 764 by 7 (the ones place digit of 397):**\n   \\[\n   764 \\times 7 = 5,\\!348\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 764 by 90 (the tens place digit of 397):**\n   \\[\n   764 \\times 90 = 68,\\!760\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 764 by 300 (the hundreds place digit of 397):**\n   \\[\n   764 \\times 300 = 229,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   5,\\!348 + 68,\\!760 + 229,\\!200 = 303,\\!308\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 764 and 397 is \\(\\boxed{303,\\!308}\\).", "292,318.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nStarting over, multiplying 764 by 7 gives 5,348.\n\nMultiplying 764 by 90 gives 68,760.\n\nMultiplying 764 by 300 gives 229,200.\n\nAdding these together: 5,348 + 68,760 equals 74,108. Then, adding 229,200 to 74,108 results in 303,308.\n\nHmm, that's different from my initial conclusion. I must have made a mistake in my first calculation. The correct total should be 303,308.\n"]]
