      "text": "92,340.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me double-check my calculations.\n\nStarting over, multiplying 405 by 8 gives 3,240.\n\nMultiplying 405 by 20 gives 8,100.\n\nMultiplying 405 by 200 gives 81,000.\n\nAdding these together: 3,240 + 8,100 = 11,340; then 11,340 + 81,000 = 92,340.\n\nHmm, that still gives me 92,340. But I think I made a mistake in the initial step. Let me try another approach.\n\nAlternatively, I can break down 228 into 200 + 20 + 8.\n\nMultiplying 405 by 200 gives 81,000.\n\nMultiplying 405 by 20 gives 8,100.\n\nMultiplying 405 by 8 gives 3,240.\n\nAdding these together: 81,000 + 8,100 = 89,100; then 89,100 + 3,240 = 92,340.\n\nWait, I'm getting the same result again. Maybe I was correct the first time. Let me verify using another method.\n\nI can also use the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 405 by 228:\n\nFirst, multiply 405 by 8: 405 \u00d7 8 = 3,240.\n\nNext, multiply 405 by 20: 405 \u00d7 20 = 8,100.\n\nThen, multiply 405 by 200: 405 \u00d7 200 = 81,000.\n\nAdding these together: 3,240 + 8,100 = 11,340; then 11,340 + 81,000 = 92,340.\n\nIt seems consistent. Therefore, the correct product of 405 and 228 is 92,340.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 405 and 228?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of 405 and 228 step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 405 by 8 (the ones place of 228):**\n   \\[\n   405 \\times 8 = 3,\\!240\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 405 by 20 (the tens place of 228):**\n   \\[\n   405 \\times 20 = 8,\\!100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 405 by 200 (the hundreds place of 228):**\n   \\[\n   405 \\times 200 = 81,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   3,\\!240 + 8,\\!100 + 81,\\!000 = 92,\\!340\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 405 and 228 is \\(\\boxed{92,\\!340}\\).",
